Z||000002||EdsB52||08-07-2000||06:43 PM||||I bet the Fiero chassis / body could handle more than 150. Besides, 150 is fast, but lets be realistic, it's not that fast. Go to any racetrack and even the 600cc motorcycles in box-stock form are doing that. We used to go on sportbike runs and maintain 120 most of the time, while occassionally topping out at 170 indicated (150 mph really). We would do this wheel to wheel many times, where small rocks comming off the bike in front of you feel like I imagine a .22 would feel. It almost sounded as if your friend was being so semantic as to say "watch out John Glenn."||||reg||1
