Z||000006||EdsB52||08-07-2000||11:46 PM||||Don't be brash Old (Fe) Lar. And why don't you reread what I posted instead of demanding I do. I wrote;<P>"We used to go on sportbike runs and maintain 120 most of the time, while occassionally topping out at 170 indicated (150 mph really)."<P>Now don't you feel foolish? I wrote runs, not races, as on tracks. Oh sure, I was previously talking about races, but I switched over to an example where I went on bike runs with other guys and we went, what you would call fast. A reasonable person would not confuse runs with races. They would draw a clear distinction between them. Should I create a new paragraph whenever I segue from a specific area of an issue to another area of that same issue, so you aren't confused?<P>Here, I'll do it. I'm not calling your buddy a pussy or anything, but 150 mph is not blinding speed. How about an analogy, shall we. 150 mph is to blinding speed:: Is as a guy worth $1,000,000 is to: rich. If you don't understand the analogy, get someone to explain it to you.<P>Changing areas within the issue. It's as if you're celebrating those guys deaths who died running into the signs. Compassion is not your strong suit.<P>Old Fellar wrote;<P>"In the past week we've had two sport bike freaks dump their bike at high speed on public roads. Flying through sign posts and getting split in two. They were only doing 85. Great public road travel. Darwin's theory come through. More power than brains."<P>Let's see, these sportbike guys were supposedly going 85 mph. Your friend who knew the corrupt pigs that allowed him to drive 150 mph on public roads, while they clocked him with City /County / State / Federal property were guilty of "Great public road travel." I'm not dealing with a refined mentality in you when I converse with you through this medium, am I?||||reg||1
