Z||000019||filthyscarecrow||08-09-2000||03:49 AM||||i read an article once where mario andretti was taking the fastest cars in the world at i think texas motorspeedway and pushing them to the limits. what does this have to do with a 150mph fiero you ask? well, when he drove the mclaren he brought it back in after a lap of about 170 and said it didn't feel right. the front camber was off by like 2 degrees. now if 2 degrees gets mario scared to drive a million dollar supercar at the limit, i see no reason why a sane person would push a fiero past 130. on a 14 year old car there's always the potential for a balljoint to slip or give out. and fiero suspension isn't as adjustable as that of the mclaren. nor is it rustproof titanium. the bottom line? i wouldn't trust it going that fast no matter how fond of the car i am. not unless it was fully race prepared with coil overs and something other than stamped steel a-arms...  <P>------------------<BR>me go fast.||||reg||1
