Z||000022||lou_dias||08-09-2000||12:39 PM||||Here is my math:<BR>Stock tire redline in first is 36mph.<BR>With 225/60/15's it is 38mph calculated by the different circumference ratios.<BR>At 3000 rpms, I do 88mph on the speedo in 5th gear.Gt 5spd<P>4800/3000 (rpm factor) * 88mph (cross multiplication) = 140.8<BR>140.8 mph * (38/36) - the new tire ratio = <BR>148.62 mph before I had to hit the brakes.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Shaun41178||08-09-2000||03:15 PM||||I have run a 14.1 at 90 mph at my local dragstrip.  That was with a 1.8 60' and a 8.8 1/8th mile with plain jane 215/60/14 street tires.<P>Mods at the time included a Nos kit jetted to 90 hp shot, underdrive pulley, crane ignition, and ported stock exhaust manifolds with a internally stock 2.8 too.  I can't wait to see what my 3.2 will do with nitrous.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
